From 03800b69d665850b769146d2e02440acaf934699 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dynfer <denesius20@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 12:42:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] g0: pause PWM for stopped frequencies and follow global
 enable

Treat NaN and nonnegative sub-1 Hz frequencies as paused PWM, retain duty for resume and honor logical inactive polarity. Keep negative, infinite and over-range frequencies invalid. Route initial G0 pause values before the generic low-frequency rejection.

Reapply active PWM setpoints against the engine PWM enable flag before each background SPI frame. This propagates disable/restore without requiring another controller callback and leaves static GPIO independent. Cover paused startup, inversion, disabled updates, late startup and deinitialization in adapter regressions.
---
 firmware/CHANGELOG.md                         |  1 +
 .../system/timer/pwm_generator_logic.cpp      | 10 +--
 firmware/hw_layer/g0_extension/README.md      |  7 +-
 .../hw_layer/g0_extension/output_gpio.cpp     | 34 +++++--
 firmware/hw_layer/g0_extension/output_gpio.h  |  1 +
 firmware/hw_layer/g0_extension/service.cpp    |  2 +
 .../hw_layer/g0_extension/tests/mocks/pch.h   |  6 ++
 .../g0_extension/tests/test_output_gpio.cpp   | 89 +++++++++++++++----
 8 files changed, 117 insertions(+), 33 deletions(-)

diff --git a/firmware/CHANGELOG.md b/firmware/CHANGELOG.md
index cdb9a92e0c..80573a035c 100644
--- a/firmware/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/firmware/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -70,6 +70,7 @@ or
  - Instant RPM is now used automatically on triggers with 24 or more teeth per engine cycle (a 12 tooth crank wheel or better), instead of only when "Always use instant RPM" was enabled. RPM, and everything derived from it, now responds within a fraction of an engine cycle instead of once per cycle. The setting remains, and now forces instant RPM on triggers with fewer teeth than that.
 
 ### Fixed
+ - G0 PWM accepts paused frequency values used by tachometer/speedometer outputs and follows the global PWM enable setting.
  - Keep configured SPI5 thermocouples deselected during G0 initialization and firmware upload on Atlas.
  - Reset G0 after firmware upload, avoid scheduler-tick delays per SPI byte, and show upload activity while yielding to other threads.
  - Changing or clearing the MAP 2, MAF, MAF 2 or fuel level sensor input no longer leaves the sensor reading its old pin (and the pin claimed) until the ECU is rebooted. MAF and fuel level input changes now take effect immediately, like other analog sensors
